  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Two identical wheels are placed at the top of two identical slopes as shown in the figure.\n\nWheel X slides down a frictionless slope without rotating.\n\nWheel Y rolls down the slope without slipping.\n\nWhich of the following statements are TRUE?\n1. Wheel X takes less time to reach the bottom of the slope than Wheel Y.\n2. Wheel Y takes less time to reach the bottom of the slope than Wheel X.\n3. Both Wheels take equal time to reach the bottom of the slope.\n4. Wheel X has greater total kinetic energy at the bottom of the slope than Wheel Y.\n5. Wheel Y has greater total kinetic energy at the bottom of the slope than Wheel X.\n6. Both Wheels have equal total kinetic energy at the bottom of the slope.",
    "solution": [
      4
    ],
